# s2a-core-blob-refs

- `native/core/crates/mixdog-app-server/src/lib.rs`, after `mod outgoing;`: `pub mod param_refs;`
  (param_refs.rs: trait `ParamRefs`, `install(Arc<dyn ParamRefs>)`, `expand(method, &mut params, &CancellationToken)`; a no-op until installed.)
- `native/core/crates/mixdog-core-domains/src/domains/blob.rs`, after `mod attachment;`: `mod param_refs;` and after the `pub use attachment::AttachmentSource;` line: `pub use param_refs::BlobParamRefs;`
  (param_refs.rs uses the private `store_error` of blob.rs as a child module.)
- `native/core/crates/mixdog-core-domains/Cargo.toml`, `[dependencies]`: `mixdog-app-server = { workspace = true }`
  (BlobParamRefs implements `mixdog_app_server::param_refs::ParamRefs`; mixdog-app-server dev-depends on mixdog-core-domains, a dev-dependency cycle cargo allows. Check `cargo hakari generate` and the Cargo.lock edge.)
- s2a-core-server-wiring: in `server.rs` call `crate::param_refs::expand(spec.method, &mut params, &cancel).await` on the params after `precheck` and before dispatch, answering its `CoreError` as any dispatch error; in the daemon composition call `mixdog_app_server::param_refs::install(BlobParamRefs::new(store.clone(), &tokens, &limits))`.
- SERVICE_PENDING (compose_flip.rs): no name to remove; blob refs add no protocol method.
